{"id":"mahabharata-12-101","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":101,"title":"एकाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 101 · The army in the field","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how a king who desires victory leads an army and how it should be arrayed, and Bhishma tells him of the rules of war and the army on the march. He describes how the array is made and warns against the sights and sounds of battle that frighten cowards.","kn":"ಜಯ ಬಯಸುವ ರಾಜ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಹೇಗೆ ನಡೆಸಬೇಕು, ಹೇಗೆ ವ್ಯೂಹ ರಚಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಯುದ್ಧ ನಿಯಮ, ಸೈನ್ಯ ಪ್ರಯಾಣದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವ್ಯೂಹ ರಚನೆ, ಹೇಡಿಗಳನ್ನು ಬೆದರಿಸುವ ಯುದ್ಧದ ದೃಶ್ಯ, ಶಬ್ದಗಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि विजय चाहने वाला राजा सेना को कैसे ले जाए और व्यूह कैसे बने, और भीष्म युद्ध के नियम और सेना के प्रयाण की बात बताते हैं। वे व्यूह-रचना और कायरों को डराने वाले युद्ध के दृश्यों-ध्वनियों से सावधान करते हैं।","te":"విజయం కోరే రాజు సైన్యాన్ని ఎలా నడపాలి, వ్యూహం ఎలా పన్నాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; భీష్ముడు యుద్ధ నియమాలు, సేన ప్రయాణం గురించి చెబుతాడు. వ్యూహ రచనను, పిరికివారిని భయపెట్టే యుద్ధ దృశ్యాలు, శబ్దాలను వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"வெற்றி விரும்பும் மன்னன் படையை எவ்வாறு நடத்தி, வியூகம் எவ்வாறு அமைக்க வேண்டும் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, போர் விதிகளையும் படைப் பயணத்தையும் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். வியூக அமைப்பையும் கோழைகளை அச்சுறுத்தும் போரின் காட்சிகள், ஒலிகளையும் விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"വിജയം ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്ന രാജാവ് സൈന്യത്തെ എങ്ങനെ നയിക്കുകയും അണിനിരത്തുകയും ചെയ്യണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; യുദ്ധനിയമങ്ങളും യാത്രയിലെ സൈന്യവും ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. അണിനിരത്തൽ എങ്ങനെയെന്ന് പറയുന്ന അദ്ദേഹം, ഭീരുക്കളെ ഭയപ്പെടുത്തുന്ന യുദ്ധത്തിലെ കാഴ്ചകളെയും ശബ്ദങ്ങളെയും കുറിച്ച് മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.101; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यथा जयार्थिनः सेनां नयन्ति भरतर्षभ ।\nईषद्धर्मं प्रपीड्यापि तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, tell me, grandfather, how those who seek victory lead their army, even if they must press dharma somewhat."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"सत्येन हि स्थिता धर्मा उपपत्त्या तथापरे ।\nसाध्वाचारतया केचित्तथैवौपयिका अपि ।\nउपायधर्मान्वक्ष्यामि सिद्धार्थानर्थधर्मयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some duties rest on truth, others on reasoning, some on the practice of good men, and some are merely expedient. I shall speak of the expedient duties that serve the aims of wealth and dharma."}},{"n":3,"text":"निर्मर्यादा दस्यवस्तु भवन्ति परिपन्थिनः ।\nतेषां प्रतिविघातार्थं प्रवक्ष्याम्यथ नैगमम् ।\nकार्याणां संप्रसिद्ध्यर्थं तानुपायान्निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Outlaws without restraint become highway menaces. To counter them I shall state the scriptural procedure; learn from me those means for the success of undertakings."}},{"n":4,"text":"उभे प्रज्ञे वेदितव्ये ऋज्वी वक्रा च भारत ।\nजानन्वक्रां न सेवेत प्रतिबाधेत चागताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two kinds of understanding must be known, straight and crooked, Bharata. Knowing the crooked, one should not practise it but should check it when it comes."}},{"n":5,"text":"अमित्रा एव राजानं भेदेनोपचरन्त्युत ।\nतां राजा निकृतिं जानन्यथामित्रान्प्रबाधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enemies approach a king by sowing division. A king who knows that deceit should crush his enemies accordingly."}},{"n":6,"text":"गजानां पार्श्वचर्माणि गोवृषाजगराणि च ।\nशल्यकङ्कटलोहानि तनुत्राणि मतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Armour is held to be made from the side hides of elephants, from oxen and boa skins, and from porcupine quills and iron."}},{"n":7,"text":"शितपीतानि शस्त्राणि संनाहाः पीतलोहिताः ।\nनानारञ्जनरक्ताः स्युः पताकाः केतवश्च ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Weapons should be sharpened and well drunk, armour yellow and red, and banners and standards dyed in many colours."}},{"n":8,"text":"ऋष्टयस्तोमराः खड्गा निशिताश्च परश्वधाः ।\nफलकान्यथ चर्माणि प्रतिकल्प्यान्यनेकशः ।\nअभिनीतानि शस्त्राणि योधाश्च कृतनिश्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lances, spears, swords, sharp axes, shields and hides should be prepared in numbers; weapons should be brought forward and warriors rested."}},{"n":9,"text":"चैत्र्यां वा मार्गशीर्ष्यां वा सेनायोगः प्रशस्यते ।\nपक्वसस्या हि पृथिवी भवत्यम्बुमती तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The march of an army is praised in Chaitra or Margashirsha, for then the earth has ripe crops and water."}},{"n":10,"text":"नैवातिशीतो नात्युष्णः कालो भवति भारत ।\nतस्मात्तदा योजयेत परेषां व्यसनेषु वा ।\nएतेषु योगाः सेनायाः प्रशस्ताः परबाधने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The season is neither too cold nor too hot, Bharata. So march then, or when the enemy is in distress; these are the right times to move an army against a foe."}},{"n":11,"text":"जलवांस्तृणवान्मार्गः समो गम्यः प्रशस्यते ।\nचारैर्हि विहिताभ्यासः कुशलैर्वनगोचरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A road with water and grass, level and passable, is praised, and one prepared by skilful scouts who move through forests."}},{"n":12,"text":"नव्यारण्यैर्न शक्येत गन्तुं मृगगणैरिव ।\nतस्मात्सर्वासु सेनासु योजयन्ति जयार्थिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Newcomers cannot travel through the forest as herds of deer do; so those who seek victory send scouts ahead in every army."}},{"n":13,"text":"आवासस्तोयवान्दुर्गः पर्याकाशः प्रशस्यते ।\nपरेषामुपसर्पाणां प्रतिषेधस्तथा भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A camp should have water, be a stronghold and have open space around; and the approach of enemies should be barred."}},{"n":14,"text":"आकाशं तु वनाभ्याशे मन्यन्ते गुणवत्तरम् ।\nबहुभिर्गुणजातैस्तु ये युद्धकुशला जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those skilled in war think open ground near a forest to have more advantages, for many reasons."}},{"n":15,"text":"उपन्यासोऽपसर्पाणां पदातीनां च गूहनम् ।\nअथ शत्रुप्रतीघातमापदर्थं परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It lets one set up retreats, hide the foot soldiers, and withstand the enemy, as a refuge in trouble."}},{"n":16,"text":"सप्तर्षीन्पृष्ठतः कृत्वा युध्येरन्नचला इव ।\nअनेन विधिना राजञ्जिगीषेतापि दुर्जयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the seven sages behind them, they should fight unmoving like mountains. By this method, O king, one may seek to conquer even the unconquerable."}},{"n":17,"text":"यतो वायुर्यतः सूर्यो यतः शुक्रस्ततो जयः ।\nपूर्वं पूर्वं ज्याय एषां संनिपाते युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the wind, the sun and Shukra are, there is victory; each earlier one is better when they clash, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":18,"text":"अकर्दमामनुदकाममर्यादामलोष्टकाम् ।\nअश्वभूमिं प्रशंसन्ति ये युद्धकुशला जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those skilled in war praise as horse ground one without mud, water, boundaries or clods."}},{"n":19,"text":"समा निरुदकाकाशा रथभूमिः प्रशस्यते ।\nनीचद्रुमा महाकक्षा सोदका हस्तियोधिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Level ground without water or cover is praised for chariots; low trees, thick undergrowth and water suit elephant-fighters."}},{"n":20,"text":"बहुदुर्गा महावृक्षा वेत्रवेणुभिरास्तृता ।\nपदातीनां क्षमा भूमिः पर्वतोपवनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ground with many obstacles, great trees, covered with canes and bamboos, mountain slopes and groves suits foot soldiers."}},{"n":21,"text":"पदातिबहुला सेना दृढा भवति भारत ।\nरथाश्वबहुला सेना सुदिनेषु प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"An army with many foot soldiers is firm, Bharata; one with many chariots and horses is praised in fair weather."}},{"n":22,"text":"पदातिनागबहुला प्रावृट्काले प्रशस्यते ।\nगुणानेतान्प्रसंख्याय देशकालौ प्रयोजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One with many foot soldiers and elephants is praised in the rains. Weighing these merits, he should choose place and time."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवं संचिन्त्य यो याति तिथिनक्षत्रपूजितः ।\nविजयं लभते नित्यं सेनां सम्यक्प्रयोजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who marches after such reflection, honoured by lunar day and star, and deploys his army well, always wins."}},{"n":24,"text":"प्रसुप्तांस्तृषिताञ्श्रान्तान्प्रकीर्णान्नाभिघातयेत् ।\nमोक्षे प्रयाणे चलने पानभोजनकालयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not strike the sleeping, the thirsty, the weary or the scattered; nor at times of release, marching, moving, or drinking and eating."}},{"n":25,"text":"अतिक्षिप्तान्व्यतिक्षिप्तान्विहतान्प्रतनूकृतान् ।\nसुविस्रम्भान्कृतारम्भानुपन्यासप्रतापितान् ।\nबहिश्चरानुपन्यासान्कृत्वा वेश्मानुसारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those thrown into disorder, confused, beaten or thinned, those who are secure and have just begun, or those worn out by a ruse, and those outside the camp who follow into houses, ..."}},{"n":26,"text":"पारंपर्यागते द्वारे ये केचिदनुवर्तिनः ।\nपरिचर्यावरोद्धारो ये च केचन वल्गिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...those who keep a gate passed down through generations, who attend and guard, and the boasters..."}},{"n":27,"text":"अनीकं ये प्रभिन्दन्ति भिन्नं ये स्थगयन्ति च ।\nसमानाशनपानास्ते कार्या द्विगुणवेतनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...those who break the enemy ranks and who cover the broken: these should be given the same food and drink and double wages."}},{"n":28,"text":"दशाधिपतयः कार्याः शताधिपतयस्तथा ।\nतेषां सहस्राधिपतिं कुर्याच्छूरमतन्द्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Appoint captains of ten and of a hundred, and over them make a captain of a thousand, a brave and alert man."}},{"n":29,"text":"यथामुख्यं संनिपात्य वक्तव्याः स्म शपामहे ।\nयथा जयार्थं संग्रामे न जह्याम परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Assembling them, the chiefs should say: 'We swear that, for victory in battle, we shall not abandon one another."}},{"n":30,"text":"इहैव ते निवर्तन्तां ये नः केचन भीरवः ।\nन घातयेयुः प्रदरं कुर्वाणास्तुमुले सति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Let those among us who are timid turn back here, lest they cause a breach and get us killed in the tumult."}},{"n":31,"text":"आत्मानं च स्वपक्षं च पलायन्हन्ति संयुगे ।\nद्रव्यनाशो वधोऽकीर्तिरयशश्च पलायने ॥","meaning":{"en":"'He who flees kills himself and his side in battle; flight brings loss of goods, death, ill fame and dishonour."}},{"n":32,"text":"अमनोज्ञासुखा वाचः पुरुषस्य पलायतः ।\nप्रतिस्पन्दौष्ठदन्तस्य न्यस्तसर्वायुधस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Unpleasant and joyless are the words said to a man who runs, with lips and teeth quivering, all weapons dropped."}},{"n":33,"text":"हित्वा पलायमानस्य सहायान्प्राणसंशये ।\nअमित्रैरनुबद्धस्य द्विषतामस्तु नस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"'May the same befall our foes: one who deserts helpers when life is at stake and is chased by enemies."}},{"n":34,"text":"मनुष्यापसदा ह्येते ये भवन्ति पराङ्मुखाः ।\nराशिवर्धनमात्रास्ते नैव ते प्रेत्य नो इह ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Those who turn their backs are the dregs of men, merely adding to the number; they have neither this world nor the next."}},{"n":35,"text":"अमित्रा हृष्टमनसः प्रत्युद्यान्ति पलायिनम् ।\nजयिनं सुहृदस्तात वन्दनैर्मङ्गलेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Enemies with glad hearts come out to meet the runaway, but friends come to the victor, dear sir, with salutations and blessings."}},{"n":36,"text":"यस्य स्म व्यसने राजन्ननुमोदन्ति शत्रवः ।\nतदसह्यतरं दुःखमहं मन्ये वधादपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"'The man whose misfortune his enemies applaud suffers, I think, a pain harder to bear than death."}},{"n":37,"text":"श्रियं जानीत धर्मस्य मूलं सर्वसुखस्य च ।\nसा भीरूणां परान्याति शूरस्तामधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Know that prosperity is the root of dharma and of all happiness; it leaves cowards and comes to the hero."}},{"n":38,"text":"ते वयं स्वर्गमिच्छन्तः संग्रामे त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nजयन्तो वध्यमाना वा प्राप्तुमर्हाम सद्गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'So we, wishing for heaven, give up our lives in battle; whether winning or slain, we deserve a good end.'"}},{"n":39,"text":"एवं संशप्तशपथाः समभित्यक्तजीविताः ।\nअमित्रवाहिनीं वीराः संप्रगाहन्त्यभीरवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having so sworn and given up their lives, the fearless heroes plunge into the enemy host."}},{"n":40,"text":"अग्रतः पुरुषानीकमसिचर्मवतां भवेत् ।\nपृष्ठतः शकटानीकं कलत्रं मध्यतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In front should be the troop of men with swords and shields, behind the troop of carts, and in the middle the women and camp."}},{"n":41,"text":"परेषां प्रतिघातार्थं पदातीनां च गूहनम् ।\nअपि ह्यस्मिन्परे गृद्धा भवेयुर्ये पुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To counter the enemy and to hide the foot soldiers; and even those in front should be eager for this."}},{"n":42,"text":"ये पुरस्तादभिमताः सत्त्ववन्तो मनस्विनः ।\nते पूर्वमभिवर्तेरंस्तानन्वगितरे जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those in front who are esteemed, spirited and strong-minded should advance first, and the others follow them."}},{"n":43,"text":"अपि चोद्धर्षणं कार्यं भीरूणामपि यत्नतः ।\nस्कन्धदर्शनमात्रं तु तिष्ठेयुर्वा समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even cowards should be encouraged with effort, so that they at least stand close or show their shoulders."}},{"n":44,"text":"संहतान्योधयेदल्पान्कामं विस्तारयेद्बहून् ।\nसूचीमुखमनीकं स्यादल्पानां बहुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let a few fight closely packed, or if he likes spread out the many; an array with few and many together may be needle-pointed."}},{"n":45,"text":"संप्रयुद्धे प्रहृष्टे वा सत्यं वा यदि वानृतम् ।\nप्रगृह्य बाहून्क्रोशेत भग्ना भग्नाः परा इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When battle is joined or when they are cheerful, truly or falsely they should raise their arms and cry: 'The enemy is broken, broken!'"}},{"n":46,"text":"आगतं नो मित्रबलं प्रहरध्वमभीतवत् ।\nशब्दवन्तोऽनुधावेयुः कुर्वन्तो भैरवं रवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Our friends' forces have arrived; strike without fear!' Shouting, they should run after, making a dreadful noise."}},{"n":47,"text":"क्ष्वेडाः किलकिलाः शङ्खाः क्रकचा गोविषाणिकान् ।\nभेरीमृदङ्गपणवान्नादयेयुश्च कुञ्जरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They should sound shouts, war-cries, conches, saws, cow-horns, kettledrums, drums and tabors, and make the elephants trumpet."}}]}]}